  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1480714378408-67cf0d13bc1b?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Yakuza Kiwami introduces four combat styles (Brawler, Rush, Beast, Dragon)—switch styles mid-combo with the d-pad to maintain combo strings across style boundaries.",
      "The Dragon Style is initially weak and must be upgraded through Majima Everywhere encounters; consistently fight Majima when he appears to unlock Dragon Style abilities faster.",
      "Heat Actions are combat multipliers—entering Heat mode and executing Heat Actions in every fight is more efficient than prolonged normal combos for clearing difficult encounters.",
      "Kiwami system: Majima appears in disguises throughout Kamurocho; beating each disguise variant unlocks unique Dragon Style moves that cannot be obtained otherwise.",
      "Use weapon durability management: grab enemy weapons during combat rather than depleting your own—enemies drop fresh weapons when knocked down."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "龍が如く 極には4つの戦闘スタイル（ブロウラー・ラッシュ・ビースト・龍）がある。十字キーでコンボ中にスタイルを切り替えてコンボ連携を維持する。",
      "龍のスタイルは初期は弱く、どこでも真島エンカウンターでアップグレードが必要。真島が現れたら積極的に戦い、龍スタイル技を早期解放する。",
      "怒りアクションは戦闘倍率。ヒートモードに入り全戦闘でヒートアクションを実行する方が難敵掃討には通常コンボより効率的。",
      "極システム：真島が神室町全体に変装して現れる。各変装バリアントを倒すと他では入手できない固有の龍スタイル技が解放される。",
      "武器耐久管理：戦闘中に自分の武器を消費させるより敵の武器を奪う。敵がダウンすると新鮮な武器を落とす。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Getting Started with Style Switching",
        "body": "Begin each major fight in Brawler style to read enemy attack patterns, then switch to Rush for agile opponents or Beast for armored/large enemies. Dragon style is weak early game—save it for practice rather than relying on it for difficult early fights. The style-switch mechanic fundamentally changes Kiwami from the PS2 original, making every style transition a deliberate tactical decision."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Majima Everywhere Priority",
        "body": "Majima appears as a chef, police officer, zombie, and other disguises throughout Kamurocho. The Majima Everywhere rank system progresses based on total fights; grinding specific encounter types (like the taxi or locker room Majima variants) unlocks powerful Dragon Style abilities significantly earlier than natural story progression. Prioritize Majima fights over most side content for combat power growth."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Final Chapter and Completion",
        "body": "The final boss sequence requires full Dragon Style availability; ensure you have completed sufficient Majima Everywhere rank before Chapter 10. For 100% completion, the Completion List tracks every substory, minigame, and Majima encounter; the Climax Battle series in the completion bonus unlocks harder combat scenarios that serve as the true post-game combat test."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Ignoring Majima Everywhere—Dragon Style is fundamentally weaker without its upgrades; players who skip Majima fights face a significant difficulty spike at late-game bosses.",
      "Not maintaining Heat gauge through combat—Heat Actions deal 3–5x normal damage; a fight completed without any Heat Actions leaves significant damage potential unused.",
      "Depleting personal weapon durability fighting random encounters—save good weapons for boss fights by grabbing enemy weapons in street brawls.",
      "Missing the Pocket Circuit substory chain—Pocket Circuit racing is one of the most developed minigames in Kiwami and missing it loses access to unique items.",
      "Not using the CP exchange shop—Completion Points earned from substories and Majima fights can be exchanged for powerful equipment that eases late-game fights."
